From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:39:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 372/488] V2 runner sampling: the greedy finish reads its parts
 up front; temperature in 2048-column blocks

The finish loaded and combined its row's parts in a loop of runtime length; each
lane now loads ceil(parts / 32) of them first (Triton's masked values past the
end), keyed by that count (1 or 2, both declared). Temperature divides 2048
columns a block instead of Triton's 8192: element-wise, the split is free, and
one token gets 64 blocks instead of 16.
---
 .../v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_sampling.py | 109 ++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

